cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software in your research, please cite it as below."
title: "Across-IntP — Multi-Variant Comparison Harness for the intp Interference Profiler"
abstract: >
  Nine implementation variants of intp, an interference profiler that collects
  seven metrics from the Linux kernel. Developed as part of a Master's
  dissertation on kernel instrumentation for interference profiling. The
  measured baseline (intp-baseline, v0.2) preserves the probe set of the
  original SystemTap IntP (Xavier et al., 2022) verbatim and isolates the two
  RCU-unsafe operations in a userspace helper; it serves as the legacy-faithful
  reference contract against two modern substrates, a portable C version on
  stable userspace ABIs and an eBPF/CO-RE version. The remaining variants
  (stap-2022, stap-nollc, stap-nohelper, stap-modern, ebpf-ring, bpftrace)
  document the portability and reliability cliffs and corroborate the measured
  results. Evaluates portability, overhead, and fidelity trade-offs across
  instrumentation ABIs.
